"hadiths[57]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1408,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Two words that are light on the tongue, heavy on the scale, and beloved to the Most Merciful: Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him, Glory be to Allah the Great” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1409,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""The uttering of the words: ""Subhan-Allah (Allah is free from imperfection), Al-hamdu lillah (all praise is due to Allah), La ilaha illallah (there is no true god except Allah) and Allahu Akbar (Allah is the Greatest)' is dearer to me than anything over which the sun rises."" [Muslim] ."
1410,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""He who utters a hundred times in a day these words: 'La ilaha illallahu, wahdahu la sharika lahu, lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamdu, wa Huwa 'ala kulli sha'in Qadir (there is no true god except Allah. He is One and He has no partner with Him; His is the sovereignty and His is the praise, and He is Omnipotent),' he will have a reward equivalent to that for emancipating ten slaves, a hundred good deeds will be recorded to his credit, hundred of his sins will be blotted out from his scroll, and he will be safeguarded against the devil on that day till the evening; and no one will exceed him in doing more excellent good deeds except someone who has recited these words more often than him. And he who utters: 'Subhan-Allahi wa bihamdihi (Allah is free from imperfection and His is the praise)' one hundred times a day, his sins will be obliterated even if they are equal to the extent of the foam of the ocean."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1411,"On the authority of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Whoever says, ‘There is no god but Allah, alone, with no partner. To Him belongs dominion and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things’ ten times. It is as if he freed four souls from the descendants of Ishmael” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1412,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me, ""Shall I tell you the expression that is most loved by Allah?"" It is 'Subhan-Allahi wa bihamdihi' (Allah is free from imperfection and His is the praise)'."" [Muslim] ."
1413,"On the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Purity is half of faith, and praise be to Allah fills the scale, and Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah fills - or fills - what is between the heavens and the earth” [Muslim]."
1414,"On the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: Teach me something to say. He said: “Say, ‘There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. Allah is the Greatest, and abundant praise is for Allah, and glory be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, and there is no power nor strength except in Allah, the Mighty, the Wise.’” He said, “These are for my Lord, so what is mine?” He said: “Say, O Allah, forgive me.” And have mercy on me, guide me, and provide for me.” [Muslim]"
1415,"On the authority of Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) finished his prayer, he would ask for forgiveness three times, and he would say: “O Allah, You are peace, and from You is peace. Blessed are you, O Possessor of majesty and honor.” Al-Awza’i, who was one of the narrators of the hadith, was asked: How to ask for forgiveness? He said: He says: I ask forgiveness from Allah, I ask forgiveness from Allah. [Muslim]."
1416,"Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say at the conclusion of prayer: ""La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lahu, lahul-mulku, wa lahul-hamdu, wa Huwa 'ala kulli shai'in Qadir. Allahumma la mani'a lima a'tayta, wa la mu'tiya lima mana'ta, wa la yanfa'u dhal-jaddi, minkal-jaddu (there is no true god except Allah. He is One and He has no partner with Him, His is the sovereignty and His is the praise, and He is Omnipotent. O Allah! There is no one who can withhold what You have given and none can bestow that which You hold back; and the greatness of the great will be of no avail to them against You)."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1417,"""La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lahu, lahul- mulku, wa lahul-hamdu, wa Huwa 'ala kulli shai'in Qadir. La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah. La ilaha illallahu, wa la na'budu illa iyyahu, Lahun-ni'matu, wa lahul-fadlu, wa lahuth-thana'ul-hasan. La ilaha ilallahu, mukhlisina, lahud-dina, wa lau karihal-kafirun (there is no true god except Allah; He is One. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is all praise, and He is Powerful over all things. There is no power and might except with (the help of) Allah. There is no Allah but Allah and we worship none except Him, to Him belongs the bounty and to Him belongs the grace, and to Him belongs all excellent praise; there is no deity but Allah. We reserve our devotion exclusively for Him though the disbelievers may detest it)."" Ibn Az-Zubair said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to celebrate Allah's Greatness in those terms after every Salat (prayer). [Muslim] ."
1418,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the poor immigrants came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: “The people of poverty have attained the highest ranks and lasting bliss: they pray as we pray, and they fast as we fast, and they have surplus wealth: they perform Hajj, Umrah, strive, and give in charity.” So he said: “Shall I not teach you something by which you will catch up with those who came before you, and with it you will precede those who came before them?” After you, will no one be better than you except the one who has done the same as what you have done? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “You glorify Allah (say SubhanAllah), praise Him (say Alhamdulillah), and declare His greatness (say Allahu Akbar). Behind every prayer there are thirty-three prayers. Abu Salih, the narrator, said on the authority of Abu Hurairah, when he was asked about how to mention them. He said: He says: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, and Allah is great, until there are thirty-three of them in total. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. Muslim added in his narration: So the poor immigrants returned to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: Our brothers who have wealth heard about what we did, and they did the same? So the Messenger of Allah said: “That is the grace of Allah. He gives it to whom He wills.” [Al-Dathur] is the plural of dathar - with the opening of the dal and the suffix of the triple tha’ - and Him: a lot of money."
1419,"And on his authority, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) he said: “Whoever glorifies Allah at the end of every prayer thirty-three times, praises Allah thirty-three times, glorifies Allah thirty-three times, and says at the end of a hundred: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He is powerful over all things, his sins will be forgiven, even if they are like the foam of the sea” [Muslim]"
1420,"On the authority of Ka’b bin Ujrah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) he said: “There are things that do not disappoint the one who says them - or the one who does them - after every prescribed prayer: thirty-three tasbihah, thirty-three tahmidahs, and thirty-four takbirs” [Muslim]."
1421,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to seek (Allah's) protection after prayers in these words: ""Alla-humma inni a'udhu bika minal-jubni wal- bukhl, wa a'udhu bika min an uradda ila ardhalil-'umur, wa a'udhu bika min fitnatid-dunya, wa a'udhu bika min fitnatil-qabr (O Allah, I seek refuge with You from cowardice, miserliness and from being sent back to a feeble age; and, seek refuge with You from the trials of this life and those of the grave)."" [Al- Bukhari] ."
1422,"And on the authority of Muadh, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took his hand and said: “O Muadh, by Allah, I love you.” He said: “I advise you, O Muadh, not to stop saying at the end of every prayer: O Allah, help me in remembering You, thanking You, and worshiping You well.” [Abu Dawud]"
1423,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “When one of you bears witness, let him seek refuge in Allah from four things, saying: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the torment of Hell, from the torment of the grave, from the temptation of life and death, and from the evil of the temptation of the Antichrist” [Muslim]."
1424,"When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was in Salat (prayer), he used to supplicate towards the end of prayer after Tashahhud and before the concluding salutations: ""Allahum-maghfir li ma qaddamtu wa ma akh-khartu, wa ma asrartu, wa ma a'lantu, wa ma asraftu, wa ma Anta a'lamu bihi minni. Antal-Muqqadimu, wa Antal-Mu'akh-khiru. La ilaha illa Anta (O Allah! Forgive my former and latter sins, which I have done secretly and those which I have done openly, and that I have wronged others, and those defaults of mine about which You have better knowledge than I have. You are the One who brings forward, and You are the One who delays None has the right to be worshipped but You."" [Muslim] ."
1425,"The Prophet (ﷺ) used to recite frequently in his bowing and prostration: ""Subhanak- Allahumma, Rabbana wa bihamdika. Allahum-maghfir li (O Allah! You are free from imperfection, our Lord, and with Your praise. Forgive my sins)."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1426,"On her authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say in his bowing and prostration: “Glory be to the Holy One, the Lord of the angels and the spirit” [Muslim]."
1427,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Glorify your Lord in Ruku' (bowing posture) and exert yourself in supplication in prostration. Thus your supplications are liable to be accepted."" [Muslim] ."
1428,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The closest a servant is to his Lord is when he is prostrating, so supplicate often” [Muslim]."
1429,"On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say while prostrating: “O Allah, forgive me all my sins, small and major, first and last, open and secret” [Muslim]."
1430,"On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: I missed the Prophet (ﷺ) one night, and I felt up and saw him kneeling - or prostrating - saying: “Glory be to You and with Your praise, there is no god but You.” And in a narration: So my hand fell on the soles of his feet, while he was in the mosque, and they were upright, and he was saying: “O Allah, I seek refuge in Your satisfaction from Your anger, and in Your forgiveness.” From your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from Your wrath, I cannot enumerate Your praise as You have praised Yourself.” [Muslim]."
1431,"We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when he asked, ""Is anyone of you unable to earn a thousand good deeds?"" One of those present asked: ""How can one earn thousand good deeds in a day?"" He (ﷺ) replied, ""By saying: Subhan Allah a hundred times, then one thousand good deeds will be recorded for him or one thousand sins will be blotted out from his record."" [Muslim] ."
1432,"On the authority of Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There is a charity due on every limb of any one of you: every tasbihah is a charity, every tahmidah is a charity, every tahlila is a charity, every takbeer is a charity, enjoining what is right is a charity, and forbidding what is evil is a charity, and two rak’ahs that one performs in the forenoon are sufficient for that” ((Narrated by) Muslim).."
1433,"On the authority of the Mother of the Believers, Juwayriyah bint Al-Harith, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Prophet (ﷺ) left her early morning when he prayed the morning prayer while she was in her mosque, then he returned after the sacrifice while she was sitting, and he said: “Are you still in the state in which you left?” She said: Yes, so the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “I have been after you four times three times, if you weighed what you said since today.” By their weight: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Him, the number of His creation, the satisfaction of Himself, the weight of His Throne, and the ink of His words. [Muslim]. And in his narration: Glory be to Allah, the number of His creation, Glory be to Allah, the satisfaction of Himself, Glory be to Allah, the weight of His Throne, Glory be to Allah, the ink of His words. And in Al-Tirmidhi’s narration: Shall I not teach you words? Do you say it? Glory be to Allah, the number of His creation, Glory be to Allah, the number of His creation, Glory be to Allah, the number of His creation, Glory be to Allah, the satisfaction of Himself, Glory be to Allah, the satisfaction of Himself, Glory be to Allah, the satisfaction of Himself, Glory be to Allah, the weight of His throne, Glory be to Allah, the weight of His throne, Glory be to Allah, the weight of His throne, Glory be to Allah, the ink of His words, Glory be to Allah, the ink of His words, Glory be to Allah, the ink of His words."
1434,"On the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “The example of one who remembers his Lord and the one who does not remember Him is like the living and the dead” [Al-Bukhari]. Muslim narrated it and said: “The example of the house in which Allah is remembered, and the example of the house in which Allah is not remembered, is like the living and the dead.”"
1435,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah Almighty says: I am as my servant thinks of me, and I am with him when he mentions me. If he mentions me to himself, I mention him to myself, and if he mentions me in an assembly, I mention him in a better assembly than them” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1436,"And on his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The singulars have preceded.” They said: What are the singulars, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “Those who remember Allah often” [Muslim]. It was narrated: [The singulars] with the r being stressed and softened, and the famous one that was said by the majority: the emphasis."
1437,"On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “The best remembrance is: There is no god but Allah.” Al-Tirmidhi narrated it and said it is a good hadith."
1438,"On the authority of Abdullah bin Bishr, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, the laws of Islam have become too much for me, so tell me something that I can cling to. He said: “Your tongue continues to be moist from the remembrance of Allah.” Al-Tirmidhi narrated it and said it was a good hadith."
1439,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""For him who says: 'Subhan-Allahi wa bi hamdihi (Allah is free from imperfection, and I begin with praising Him, and to Him),' a palm-tree will be planted in Jannah."" [At- Tirmidhi] ."
1440,"Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""I met Ibrahim (ﷺ) on the Night of Ascension (Al-Asra), and he said to me: 'O Muhammad, convey my greetings to your Ummah, and tell them that Jannah has a vast plain of pure soil and sweet water. It is a plain levelled land. The plants grow there by uttering: Subhan-Allah, Al-hamdu lillah, La ilaha illallah and Allahu Akbar (Allah is free from imperfection; praise be to Allah; there is no true god except Allah; and Allah is Greatest)."" [At- Tirmidhi] ."
1441,"On the authority of Abu Darda, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Shall I not inform you of the best of your deeds, the most pure in the sight of your King, the highest in your ranks, better for you than spending gold and silver, and better for you than meeting your enemy and striking their necks, and them striking your necks?” They said: Yes, he said: “He said: “Remembrance of Allah Almighty.”” Almighty.” [Al-Tirmidhi]"
1442,"And on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, that he entered with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to see a woman and in her hands were stones - or pebbles - with which she could recite the tasbih, and he said: “I will tell you what is easier for you than this - or better.” So he said: “Glory be to Allah, the number of what He created in the heavens, and Glory be to Allah, the number of what He created on earth, and Glory be to Allah, the number of what is in between, and Glory be to Allah, the number of what He is the Creator, and Allah is greater like that, and praise be to Allah. Like that, and there is no god but Allah like that, and there is no power nor strength except in Allah like that.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
1443,"On the authority of Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: “Shall I not direct you to one of the treasures of Paradise?” So I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “There is no power nor strength except with Allah” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1444,"On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to remember Allah Almighty at all times. [Muslim]"
1445,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""If anyone intends to have (sexual intercourse) with his wife, he should say: ""Bismillah! Allahumma janibnash-Shaitana, wa jannibish-Shaitana ma razaqtana (In the Name of Allah, O Allah! Keep us away from Satan and keep Satan away from what You have bestowed upon us);' and if Allah has ordained a child for them, Satan will never harm him."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1446,"On the authority of Hudhayfah and Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went to bed, he would say: “In your name, O Allah, I die and live.” And when he woke up, he would say: “Praise be to Allah who revived us after He caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection” [Al-Bukhari]."
1447,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah Almighty has angels who roam the roads seeking people of remembrance, and when they find people who remember Allah Almighty, they call out: Come to what you need, and they surround them with their wings up to the lowest heaven., and their Lord - and He knows best - asks them: What do My servants say? He said: They say: They glorify You, magnify You, praise You, and glorify You with majesty. He says: Have they seen me? They say: No, no, by Allah, they have not seen you. He says: What if they had seen me?! He said: They say: If they had seen you, they would have worshiped you more, glorified you more, and glorified you more. He says: So what do they ask? He said: They say: They ask you for Paradise. He said: He says: And did they see it? He said: They say: No, by Allah, O Lord, they did not see it. He said: He says: So what if they had seen it?! He said: They say: If they had seen it, they would have been more eager for it, more eager for it, and greater in desire for it. He said: So what do they seek refuge with? He said: They say: They seek refuge from Hell. He said: He says: Did they see it? He said: They say: No, by Allah, they did not see it. He says: What if they had seen it? He said: They say: If they had seen it, they would have fled more and feared it more. He said: He says: I bear witness that I have forgiven them. He said: One of the angels says: Among them is so-and-so who is not one of them, but he came for a need. He said: They are the companions, and their companion does not feel miserable with them. And they ascended to heaven, and Allah Almighty - and He knows best - asks them: Where did you come from? They say: We came from your servants on earth: they glorify you, glorify you, declare Your oneness., praise you, and ask you. He said: What do they ask me? They said: They ask you for your paradise. He said: And have they seen my paradise? They said: No, O Lord. He said: So how if? They saw my paradise?! They said: And they seek protection from you. He said: And from what do they seek protection from me? They said: From your fire, O Lord. He said: And did they see my fire? They said: No. He said: So what if they saw my fire? They said: And they seek your forgiveness. Then he says: I have forgiven them, and I have given them what they asked, and I granted them refuge from what they sought refuge. He said: So they say: Lord. Among them is so-and-so, a sinful servant who passed by and sat with them, and he says: “And I have forgiven him.” They are the people whose companions do not feel miserable about them.”"
1448,"On his authority and on the authority of Abu Saeed, may Allah be pleased with them, they said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “No people sit remembering Allah Almighty except that the angels surround them, and mercy envelops them and tranquility descends upon them, and Allah remembers them among those with Him” [Muslim]."
1449,"On the authority of Abu Waqid Al-Harith bin Awf, may Allah be pleased with him, that while the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was sitting in the mosque, and the people were with him, two people came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and one went and stood in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). One of them saw an opening in the circle, so he sat in it. As for the other, he sat behind them, and as for the third, he turned away and left. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) finished, He said: Shall I not tell you about the three people: As for one of them, he sought refuge with Allah, and Allah gave him shelter. As for the other, he was ashamed and Allah was ashamed of him. As for the other, he turned away, so Allah turned away from him. (Agreed upon)"
1450,"Mu'awiyah (May Allah be pleased with him) came to an assembly in the mosque and asked them: ""What has made you sit together?"" They replied, ""We are sitting here to remember Allah."" He said, ""I adjure you by Allah to tell me whether nothing else has made you to sit together."" They replied: ""By Allah! We are sitting only to remember Allah."" Then he said, ""I did not adjure you because I suspected you. No one of my rank in the eyes of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) is the narrator of so few traditions as I am. The fact is that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out to a circle of his Companions and said, 'What has made you sit there?' When they replied that they are sitting together to remember Allah and to praise Him for guiding them to Islam and bestowing favours on them, he (ﷺ) said, 'I adjure you by Allah to tell me that nothing else has made you sit together.' On their reply that there was certainly no other purpose, he (ﷺ) said, 'I did not adjure you because I suspected you, but Jibril (Gabriel) came to me and told me that Allah was talking proudly of you to the angels.""' [Muslim] ."
1451,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""He who recites in the morning and in the evening the statement: 'Subhan-Allahi wa bihamdihi (Allah is free from imperfection and I begin with praising Him)' one hundred times, will not be surpassed on the Day of Resurrection by anyone with better deeds than one who utters the same words or utters more of these words."" [Muslim] ."
1452,"On his authority, he said: A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I was stung by a scorpion yesterday! He said: “But if you had said in the evening: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created, it would not have harmed you” [Muslim]."
1453,"And on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) that he used to say when morning came: “O Allah, by you we have entered the morning, by you we have entered the evening, by you we live, by you we die, and to You is the resurrection.” And when evening came, he would say: “O Allah, by you we have entered the evening, by you we live, by you we die, and to You is the return.” [Abu Dawud]"
1454,"On his authority, Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah, give me words to say in the morning and in the evening. He said: Say: “O Allah, Creator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, Lord of everything and its Sovereign. I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of myself and the evil of Satan and his evil.” He said: “Say it in the morning, and in the evening, and when you take your bed.” [Abu Dawud]"
1455,"On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When evening came, the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) would say: “We have arrived, and the kingdom belongs to Allah at night, and praise be to Allah. There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner.” The narrator said: I see him saying in them: “To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things. My Lord, I ask you for the good of this night and the good of what comes after it, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of this night and the evil of what comes after it.” My Lord, I seek refuge in You from laziness and the evil of arrogance. My Lord, I seek refuge in You from the evil of this night and the good of what comes after it, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of this night and the evil of what comes after it. My Lord, I seek refuge in You from laziness and the evil of arrogance. My Lord, I seek refuge in You from the torment of the Fire and the torment in the grave. And when he woke up, he also said that: “We have risen in the morning and the kingdom belongs to Allah” ([Muslim].."
1456,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me, ""Recite Surat Al-Ikhlas and Al- Mu'awwidhatain (Surat Al-Falaq and Surat An-Nas) three times at dawn and dusk. It will suffice you in all respects."" [Abu Dawud and At-Tirmidhi] ."
1457,"On the authority of Othman bin Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There is no servant who says in the morning of every day and in the evening of every night: In the name of Allah, with whose name nothing on earth or in the sky can be harmed, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing, three times, except that nothing will harm him.” [Abu Dawud]"
1458,"On the authority of Hudhayfah and Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with them, that when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went to bed, he would say: “In your name, O Allah, I live and die” [Al-Bukhari]."
1459,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me and to Fatimah (May Allah be pleased with her) (Ali's wife and the Prophet's daughter), ""When you go to bed, recite: Takbir (Allahu Akbar) thirty-three times and Tasbih (Subhan-Allah) thirty-three times and Tahmid (Al-hamdu lillah) thirty-three times."" Another narration is: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""Recite Tasbih thirty-four times."" Another narration is: The Messenger of Allah(ﷺ) said, ""Recite Takbir thirty-four times."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1460,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""When any of you goes to bed, he should shake off (or dust off) his bedsheet because he does not know what might have fallen on it after he had left it. Then he should recite: 'Bismika Rabbi wada'tu janbi, wa bika arfa'uhu, in amsakta nafsi farhamha, wa in arsaltaha fahfazha bima tahfazu bihi 'ibadakas-salihin [With Your Name, my Rubb, I place my side (upon the bed) and with Your Grace I will raise it up. If You withhold my soul (cause me to die), have mercy on it but if You let it go (let me live), guard it against which You guarded Your pious slaves] .""' [Al- Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1461,"On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went to bed, he would blow on his hands, recite al-Mu’awwidhat (the two protective chapters)t (the two protective chapters), and wipe his body with them. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in their narration: “When the Prophet (ﷺ) went to bed every night, he would put his palms together, then blow on them, and recite in them: Say, ‘He is Allah, One,’” And say: ‘I seek refuge in the Lord of the Dawn (Al-Falaq)’, and say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind. Then he wiped with them as much of his body as he could, starting with them on his head and face, and the front of his body. He did that three times. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. The linguists said: [nafth] is gentle blowing without saliva"
1462,"On the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: “When you go to your bed, perform your ablution for prayer, then lie down on your right side, and say: O Allah, I have surrendered myself to You, turned my face to You, entrusted my affairs to You, and turned my back to You out of desire and fear for You. There is no refuge or escape from You except to You. I have believed in Your Book which You have revealed, and in Your Prophet whom You have sent. If you die, die upon the innate nature of Islam (fitrah), and make them the last thing you say.” (Agreed upon)"
1463,"And on the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that when the Prophet (ﷺ) went to bed, he would say: “Praise be to Allah who fed us and gave us drink, and sufficed us and sheltered us. How many are there who have no one to suffice them (provide for their needs) and no one to give them shelter/abode?” [Muslim]."
1464,"On the authority of Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, that when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wanted to lie down, he would place his right hand under his cheek, then say: “O Allah, protect me from Your torment on the day You resurrect Your servants.” [It was narrated by Al-Tirmidhi and he said it is a good hadith. It was narrated by Abu Dawud from the narration of Hafsa, may Allah be pleased with him, and it says that he used to say it three times]."
